<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				plunderer</i>, <i>pillager.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quos ego in eodem genere praedatorum
					direptorumque pono,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 2, 9, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercitus, praedator ex sociis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 44, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A hunter</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedator aprorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 306</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4, 316</span></i>.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a ravisher</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 85, 3</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A rapacious</i> or <i>avaricious
			man</i>, <i><span class="en">Tib. 2, 3, 43</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
